  §16.5: body_range (4449, 4471)  section_span (4449, 4482)  DIFFER   [L9193 cites it for totality: "every claim supported, cited, or marked open"]
  --- §16.5 body L4449-L4470 ---
   4449 ### 16.5 D3 — totality catches a missing value
   4450     Theorem. If Λ is closed, χ_Λ : ∏Aᵢ → {0,1} is total: membership is decided for every ambient point
   4451     by a finite conjunction of decidable comparisons. Proof. Each bound compares two elements of a
   4452     chain. Λ is a finite intersection of such conditions. ∎
   4453 
   4454  **Verified on every ambient point — all 6,912 of them, χ ∈ {0,1} everywhere, nothing undecided, and
   4455  χ agreeing with membership on every cell.** An earlier pass drew 30,000 uniform samples from a box of
   4456  6,912, which is more draws than cells and still not a proof of totality; the exhaustive test costs
   4457  less than the sampling did. Register 248.
   4458 
   4459  **Worked case.** A species was misidentified — Na II read as neutral neon, and the wrong ionisation limit applied. Every channel had *T* = *I* − *E* ≤ 0 and **every one was refused at entry.**
   4460 
   4461     Totality does not detect that error. It forbids it. The computation never ran.
   4462 
   4463  **Worked case, the other way.** A guard in the author's code returned `None` when an alphabet exceeded a cap, and the caller coerced `None` to `False`. That produced "3 reorderable of 85 trials," which produced "almost never reorderable," which produced a false dismissal of an entire line of evidence.
   4464 
   4465     One silent discard propagated through three conclusions, none of which looked wrong,
   4466     because the arithmetic was consistent throughout.
   4467 
   4468  ⅅ ≥ 1 cannot catch that. Every relation checks out on data that was never measured. Only totality
   4469  closes the hole, because undetermined is not in the codomain.
   4470 

  §16.3: body_range (4359, 4379)  section_span (4359, 4407)  DIFFER   [L9201 cites it for D_phys]
  --- §16.3 body L4359-L4378 ---
   4359 ### 16.3 D1 — D_phys catches a wrong value in the data
   4360  Worked case. Two species in this work, Al II and K II, were first computed with Z_eff = 1. Both have
   4361  doubly charged cores.
   4362 
   4363     The bracket held 56 of 56 either way. Containment depends only on monotonicity of T, and Z
   4364     cancels from it entirely.
   4365 
   4366  What failed were the quantities the method does not use. δ̄ came out near 4.9 with a spread of several units — impossible for a Rydberg series, where δ is near-constant. *V* departed from 4ν/3 by a **median of 50%**, where Na I gives 0.2%.
   4367 
   4368  Corrected to *Z*_eff = 2: δ̄ = 1.271 with spread 0.047 over ten members, and *V* to **0.86%** across the fifty cells.
   4369 
   4370     The bracket verifies the data. V verifies the indexing. An index carrying only what its method
   4371     consumes would have passed fifty-six wrong cells.
   4372 
   4373 ![Figure 16.1](figures/figure-16.1.png)
   4374 
   4375  Figure 16.1. The bracket holds fifty-six of fifty-six under either charge, because Z cancels from containment. The defect
   4376  does not: at Z = 1 it spreads over several units, which no Rydberg series can do. The method was blind; a quantity the
   4377  method never uses was not.
   4378 

  §6.3: body_range (1705, 1718)  section_span (1705, 1718)  COINCIDE   [L9285 cites it for the calendar, "E = 7 is the price of keeping January first"]
  --- §6.3 body L1705-L1717 ---
   1705 ### 6.3 The calendar can be repaired, and the repair is instructive
   1706  The calendar fails for one reason: days(m) is not monotone in m, because February has 28. Relabel the
   1707  months in order of length — February, April, June, September, November, January, March, … — and E
   1708  drops to 0. The 365 cells are identical; only the labels move.
   1709 
   1710  **And the repaired calendar is useless.** A calendar whose months run in order of length is self-defining and unusable.
   1711 
   1712  So the trade is explicit, and it has a number:
   1713 
   1714       E(X) = 7 is the price of keeping January first.
   1715 
   1716  Non-closure is not always a fault. It is sometimes a purchase — usability bought with definitional self-sufficiency. What this book supplies is the price tag, not the verdict.
   1717 

